From a6395efbb61b5c3a741cfd309a2d3e620c2df01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai <kai@organicemperor.local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:28:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] SEO: server-render article bodies into archives shells +
 sitemap/robots

Post pages served via the Django shell pipeline now include the full
article text (title, byline, excerpt, blocks) inside #app, so crawlers
receive real content instead of an empty Vue mount point. The Vue app
still replaces it on mount; behavior for JS visitors is unchanged.

- backend/config/seo.py: render_post_body()/render_block() with
  conservative dependency-free Markdown subset; all user content escaped.
  html_response() injects body HTML into <div id="app">. New
  archives_sitemap and archives_robots views (no-store).
- backend/config/urls.py: routes for the new views.
- frontend/public/.htaccess: proxy sitemap.xml/robots.txt to Django on the
  archives host instead of serving the SPA shell.
- backend/config/test_seo.py: 4 new tests (body content, XSS escaping,
  no body on 404/product pages, sitemap/robots).
